NOT YET CHOSEN — and blocked on a specific question, not on indecision.

The code licence for this repository cannot be settled independently of the
checkpoint licences it depends on. Decision D-046 established that release is
stratified rather than uniform:

  Tier A  unrestricted        Apache-2.0 / MIT checkpoints
  Tier B  conditional         DINOv3 (notice required), MoCo v3 (CC-BY-NC-4.0)
  Tier C  withheld            UNI (CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0), MONET (CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0)

Two consequences:

1. Three of the ten backbones are NON-COMMERCIAL. Whatever licence this code
   carries, artifacts derived from those backbones are non-commercial only.

2. MONET is CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0, a ShareAlike licence. Whether an adapter trained on
   MONET embeddings, or the embeddings themselves, constitute "Adapted Material"
   under Creative Commons is an unsettled legal question, and this project does
   not assert an answer. Pending institutional guidance, MONET-derived artifacts
   are withheld as a precaution rather than released under an asserted licence.

Until that question is answered, no licence is asserted here. This is a recorded
open item (D-046), not an oversight.

NOTE: a code licence would in any case cover the CODE only. It grants no rights
over ISIC 2019, PAD-UFES-20, or any pretrained checkpoint, each of which carries
its own terms. Those are recorded in assets/README.md.
